# Project-scoped Firebase Functions params for blueseal-762af.
# firebase-functions params (defineString) read this file at deploy time, in
# addition to the gitignored local functions/.env used for `npm run dev:full`.
#
# Committed on purpose: these are Stripe PRICE IDs (product identifiers), which
# are NOT secret — they're visible in the Stripe Checkout URL. CI does a clean
# checkout that does NOT include the gitignored functions/.env, so without this
# file a non-interactive `firebase deploy --only functions` fails with:
#   "no value for ... STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY, STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_ANNUAL"
# (production CI failure, 2026-06-12).
#
# Genuinely secret values (STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET, the Google
# OAuth secrets) are NOT here — they live in Google Secret Manager via
# defineSecret() and are granted to the CI service account by IAM.
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY=price_1U6HjoEfjKnllaHjLC5Xs7aN
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_ANNUAL=price_1U6HjoEfjKnllaHjDOXaaFGm
# OFF since the live-Stripe cutover (2026-08-19). qaSetSelfPro /
# qaProvisionSelf* can fabricate an approved tradesperson and grant Blue Seal
# Pro with no Stripe involved — a billing bypass once real money moves. The qa
# role alone still gates "Reset my data" (resetSelfData is not env-gated), so
# testers keep that.
QA_TOOLKIT_ENABLED=false
